# clause-typecheck — Design

Type checking, generic resolution, coherence checking, bind-target
resolution, and the validator framework. Consumes a resolved
program graph from clause-resolve; produces a typed graph.

## Scope

- `TypeChecker` — top-level state + drive loop.
- `TypeEnv` — type environment per scope.
- `Generics` — generic parameter handling, substitution, bounds.
- `Coherence` — overlap detection for trait impls.
- `BindTarget` — resolution of target-language types (generic
  scaffolding; concrete targets land in clause-jomini and friends
  via the extension point from R3).
- **Validator framework** — the R4-scoped framework lives here.
  R4 decides the concrete Rust shape (tagged-union trait? compile-
  time dispatch? plugin registry?) and which validators live in
  core vs plugins.
- Type diagnostics.

## Non-scope

- Pass DAG scheduling (clause-schedule).
- Codegen (clause-codegen).
- Concrete target bind-table content (extension crates).

## Dependencies

- `clause-ir`, `clause-syntax`, `clause-resolve`.
- arvo for numeric / newtype discipline.
- arvo-bitmask for validator access sets (one validator ↔ one
  AccessSet over Namespace/Scope entries).
- `#![no_std]`, no alloc.

## Provisional module layout

- `checker.rs` — top-level TypeChecker + drive loop.
- `env.rs` — TypeEnv.
- `generics.rs` — generic param handling.
- `coherence.rs` — overlap detection (also available as a core
  Validator).
- `bind_target.rs` — target-language type resolution scaffolding.
- `validator/` — framework subtree (R4 finalised shape):
  - `trait.rs` — Validator trait, Category enum.
  - `registry.rs` — ValidatorRegistry const-sized array +
    register / get / iter.
  - `ctx.rs` — ValidatorCtx (typecheck state + workspace +
    suppression map accessors).
  - `suppression.rs` — attribute parsing + crate config lookup.
  - `severity.rs` — Category → Severity mapping.
  - `builtin/` — shipped validators:
    - `strict1_no_shadow.rs`
    - `strict2_unused.rs`
    - `strict3_assign_to_immut.rs`
    - `strict4_int_overflow.rs`
    - `strict5_use_after_move.rs`
    - `strict6_ambiguous_imports.rs`
    - `strict7_clippy_batch.rs`
    - `coherence.rs` — overlap detection as a Validator wrapper.
    - `orphan_rule.rs`
    - `bind_target_shape.rs`
- `diagnostics.rs` — type error construction.

## Validator framework (R4, finalised 2026-04-26)

`Validator` is a trait; `ValidatorRegistry` is const-sized
`[Option<&'static dyn Validator>; MAX_VALIDATORS]`. Same sanctioned
`&'static dyn` exception as clause-codegen's TargetRegistry —
confined to registry iteration surface, static-lifetime.

```rust
pub trait Validator: Sized + Send + Sync + 'static {
    const NAME: &'static str;
    const CATEGORY: Category;

    fn accepts(&self, kind: AstNodeKind) -> bool;
    fn check(
        &self,
        node: &TypedNode,
        ctx: &ValidatorCtx<'_>,
        sink: &mut DiagnosticSink,
    );
}

pub enum Category {
    Strict,       // STRICT1-7; default Error severity.
    Type,         // coherence, orphan-rule, bind-target-shape.
    Style,        // default Warning.
    Performance,  // default Info.
    Custom,       // consumer-defined; trait provides default.
}
```

Core validators ship with the crate:
- STRICT1 `no-shadow`
- STRICT2 `unused`
- STRICT3 `assign-to-immut`
- STRICT4 `int-overflow`
- STRICT5 `use-after-move`
- STRICT6 `ambiguous-imports`
- STRICT7 `clippy-batch`
- `coherence`, `orphan-rule`, `bind-target-shape`.

Plugin validators register via `ValidatorRegistry::register` from
consumer build-scripts / main functions. No compile-time magic.

Suppression tiers: per-item `#[allow / warn / deny]` attributes on
AST nodes → per-crate `[lints]` in Clause.toml → per-workspace
`[workspace.lints]` → Category default severity.

Scheduling: `clause-schedule` walks validators per AST node via
`accepts(kind)`. Sequential per-node; parallelisable across nodes
as a future optimisation.

